      ":question/id": "1f281aba-5807-5add-afd7-ec83d61c5b06",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-100748",
      ":question/problem": "${\\left(-\\frac{2}{5}\\right)}^{2}=$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, notice that $-\\frac{2}{5}=\\frac{(-2)}{5}.$\n\nTo raise the fraction to the power of $2$, we must raise both the numerator and the denominator to the power of $2:$\n\n$$\n{\\left(-\\frac{2}{5}\\right)}^{2}={\\left(\\frac{(-2)}{5}\\right)}^{2}=\\frac{(-2)^{2}}{{5}^{2}}\n$$\n\nNow, using $(-2)^{2}=4$ and ${5}^{2}=25,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{(-2)^{2}}{{5}^{2}}=\\frac{4}{25}.\n$$"
    }
