      ":question/id": "19d50236-91d2-5a2a-a9cb-16ff563fb6a3",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-68464",
      ":question/problem": "$6{\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)}^{3}=$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To raise the fraction to the power of $3$, we must raise both the numerator and the denominator to the power of $3.$ So we have\n\n$$\n{\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)}^{3}=\\frac{{2}^{3}}{{3}^{3}}=\\frac{8}{27}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n6{\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)}^{3}=6\\cdot \\frac{8}{27}=\\frac{48}{27}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify:\n\n$$\n\\frac{48}{27}=\\frac{16\\cdot 3}{9\\cdot 3}=\\frac{16}{9}\n$$"
    }
